# Building an image

Build with the image in `README.md`:

```bash
docker run -it --rm -v "$(pwd)":/workdir \
  ghcr.io/openvario/ovbuild-container:latest --workdir=/workdir
```

Inside the container, BitBake is not on `PATH` until the environment
script runs:

```bash
source openembedded-core/oe-init-build-env .
export MACHINE=ov-cb2-ch57
bitbake openvario-image
```

- `MACHINE` must be an `ov-*` machine from `conf/machine/`. The sample
  default is `ov-cb2-pq70`. Export the board you mean.
- Common targets: `openvario-image`, `openvario-image-testing`,
  `openvario-recovery-image`.
- The container user is the owner of `/workdir`. Do not run BitBake as
  root, and do not `docker exec` as root to create files the build
  writes.
- Output is `tmp/deploy/images/${MACHINE}/`. The disk image is
  `OV-<version>.img.gz`. It is the whole card, including the bootloader.
- `tmp/` is tens of gigabytes. Do not point `TMPDIR` at `/tmp`.
- Keep `downloads/` and `sstate-cache/` across rebuilds. They are safe
  to delete only when you mean to fetch and compile again.
- A non-interactive run drops `-it` and passes the shell command after
  the image name. `oe-init-build-env` must still be sourced in that
  shell.
